# Every typed absence as its document filed it. One row per absent element: where it sits, the
# layer it sits in, the reason, the note that argues for it, the date it holds at, and who
# declined and on what standing.
#
# The relation for the type, beside the census for the questions
#   epistemics/absences.sqlc asks each question of the column that answers it, and that column
#   holds the reason alone. This is the same set of absences read from the elements, with
#   everything a filer wrote beside the reason. Most carry a note, and the note is where a
#   document says why it could not answer: `refutation/object-storage` files its denied remainder
#   as a counter-example "not as a gap in this document".
#
# `owns` joins it to the claim at the same position
#   It is spelled as epistemics/claims.sqlc spells it, `parent/wrapper`, so a position's claims
#   and its absences are one join apart.
-- pm:Absence and pm:ClaimAbsence, every one, with pm:note, pm:asOf and pm:provenance.
SELECT a.filing, a.seq, a.owns, a.layer, a.reason, a.note, a.as_of,
       a.prov_party, a.prov_entered_by, a.prov_approved_by,
       a.prov_standing_taxonomy, a.prov_standing_value, a.prov_standing_absent, a.prov_note
FROM pm.absence a
